system "ISO:rus-Cyrl:Latn:9-2026" {

metadata {
  authority_id iso
  id 9-2026
  language iso-639-2:rus
  source_script Cyrl
  destination_script Latn
  name "ISO/FDIS 9:2026 Information and documentation -- Transliteration of Cyrillic characters into Latin characters -- Slavic and non-Slavic languages (Russian) (FDIS stage)"
  url https://www.iso.org/committee/48820.html
  creation_date 2026
  description {    Third edition (FDIS stage) of ISO 9, Transliteration of Cyrillic characters into
    Latin characters. Table 1 encodes all 168 main rows (upper and lower case
    where given; rows 158-159 are caseless), Table 2 the 15 rare-or-obsolete
    rows (lower case only), and the clause 4.4 formula example. Hex columns of
    the source table are authoritative over printed glyphs.
  }

  notes {
  note "Encoded from ISO/FDIS 9:2026, ISO/TC 46/WG 3 N127 (FDIS ballot; document date 2026-10-26, id 89763). FDIS stage: verify against the published edition when available."
  note "Source footnote b: rows 138, 143 and 168 normally transliterate with the lower-case form only; where an upper-case distinction is needed a prefixed circumflex U+02C6 is added (encoded as the printed upper-case forms)."
  note "Source footnote a: row 97 (OE ligature) has no encoding in the Cyrillic block; the Latin-block codepoints 0152/0153 serve both sides."
  note "Against the 2nd edition (1995), combining comma below U+0326 is replaced by combining cedilla U+0327 throughout (rows 38 43 60 79 105 109 124 132 167); rows 68 78 87 115 116 152 165 166 are changed or reassigned per the source's informative type column."
  note "Clause 4.1.2 (precomposed and decomposed characters treated equally on input): each precomposed Cyrillic letter with a canonical Unicode decomposition additionally carries a companion rule keyed on its decomposed sequence, mapping to the same output."
  note "Clause 4.4 (unlisted Cyrillic + combining mark -> Latin + U+005F LOW LINE + combining mark) is not generically expressible in the stateless longest-match rule engine; only the clause's own worked example (0451+0301 -> 00EB+005F+0301, plus its decomposed twin per 4.1.2) is encoded as a rule."
  note "Table 2 rows are transcribed verbatim by hex code; several printed Latin outputs do not follow the clause 4.4 pattern (e.g. row 170: 0456+0304+0307 -> 0069+0306; rows 169/171/172/174/175/177/179/181) - encoded as printed, pending the published edition."
  note "Case-asymmetric rows as printed: row 56 upper 004A+030C / lower 01F0 precomposed; row 127 upper 0048+0331 / lower 1E96 precomposed."
  }
}
